mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D44F TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>. The\nintegral is then said to <strong>converge</strong>.</p>","file":"ch21-inequalities/10-loewners-theorem.html"}